### Order.Api - manual test flow
### Works out of the box: no external Identity server needed (see /api/v1/dev/token).
### In Visual Studio / Rider: click "Send Request" above each block.
### In VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request".

@host = http://localhost:5080
@userId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### 1. Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. Get a dev JWT for a test user (Development environment only)
# Run this first, then copy the "token" value from the response into @token below.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/dev/token?userId={{userId}}

### 3. Set the token from step 2 here
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2_HERE

### 4. Create an order (Idempotency-Key prevents duplicate orders on retry)
# Product id/price/name come from Catalog now - the client only sends productId + quantity.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-checkout-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
      "quantity": 1
    },
    {
      "productId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 5. Re-send the same request with the same Idempotency-Key
### -> should return the SAME order instead of creating a new one
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-checkout-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 6. Get my orders (cached for 30 seconds)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get a single order by id
# Replace {orderId} with the "id" returned from step 4.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{orderId}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Move the order forward: PendingPayment -> Paid
# Replace {orderId} with the "id" returned from step 4.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{orderId}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Paid"
}

### 9. Try an invalid transition on purpose (Paid -> Shipped is not allowed)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request with a clear error message.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{orderId}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Shipped"
}

### 10. Try reading orders without a token
# Expected: 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders

### 11. Try ordering a product that doesn't exist in Catalog
# Expected: 400 Bad Request.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-checkout-bad-product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}
